#13 MPW readiness: cut-down configuration without the vector unit (SIGIL_NO_VECTOR)
Date: 2026-10-24 (UTC). Branch 13-mpw-novec, from main 3b7ed1b.
Last RTL change: 6eb9727 (every RTL-dependent gate below ran at or after it;
later commits touch scripts, Makefiles' comments, CI and docs only).

Owner decision (2026-10-24): the MPW version may drop the vector unit and keep
everything else (RV64GC + B + K + H, FPU, MMU, caches, crypto engine).

== What changed
- rtl/core/sigil_pkg.sv: SIGIL_NO_VECTOR is read once -> localparam
  HAS_VECTOR (1 by default). Every use is a constant condition.
- rtl/core/sigil_core.sv: sigil_vregfile + sigil_vec in generate block g_vec
  (paths u_core.g_vec.u_vregfile / u_core.g_vec.u_vec), outputs tied to 0 in
  g_novec; vec_unit_op, vset_en and vls_is gated with HAS_VECTOR;
  sigil_csr #(.HAS_VECTOR(HAS_VECTOR)).
- rtl/core/sigil_decoder.sv: !HAS_VECTOR -> every vector encoding invalid
  (OP-V incl. vset{i}vl{i}, vector LS in LOAD-FP/STORE-FP widths
  000/101/110/111) -> illegal-instruction, mtval = encoding.
- rtl/core/sigil_csr.sv: parameter HAS_VECTOR; without it vstart, vxsat, vxrm,
  vcsr, vl, vtype, vlenb do not exist, misa = 0x8000_0000_0014_11AF (no V),
  mstatus.VS / sstatus.VS / vsstatus.VS read 0 (writes ignored, not in SD).
- rtl/sigil_soc_files.mk: SIGIL_SOC_DEFINES_NOVEC / SIGIL_SOC_DEFINES,
  SIGIL_SKY130_{VRF,L1}_MACROS, SIGIL_SKY130_MACROS (VRF macro dropped with
  SIGIL_NO_VECTOR=1), SIGIL_FAKERAM45_VRF_MACROS.
- flow/designs/{sky130hd,nangate45}/sigil_soc/config.mk: SIGIL_NO_VECTOR=1
  adds -DSIGIL_NO_VECTOR and drops the VRF macro LEF/LIB/GDS/model.
  nangate45 sta_synth.tcl: vector-unit path u_cpu/u_core/g_vec/u_vec.
- Makefile lint: + sigil_core, sigil_cpu (+COMMIT_TRACE), sigil_soc_top
  (default, sky130 MPW without the VRF model, nangate45 without the VRF
  model) and sigil_fpga_top, all with SIGIL_NO_VECTOR (26 invocations).
- sim/Makefile: families novec / sky130novec (core_tb_*, soc_rtl_tb_*),
  soc_tb_novec, core-novec (in `all` = make core-test), core-novec-quick
  (CI), riscv-tests-novec, novec-bins (build/sim/novec/*.bin with
  -DSIGIL_NO_VECTOR); VEC_TESTS / NOVEC_TESTS / NOVEC_RUN_TESTS.
- sim/run_directed.sh: NOVEC=1 -> novec/ binaries, VEC_TESTS skipped,
  novec_trap_directed added. (irq_exc_race coverage file now honours
  COV_PREFIX like the other loops.)
- sw/core-tests/novec_trap_directed.S (new); md_directed, md_kill_directed,
  fp_stall_directed, mmio_bypass_directed, pmp_modes_directed and
  priv_directed guard their vector sections / misa value with
  #ifdef SIGIL_NO_VECTOR (md_kill: a scalar faulting load replaces the vector
  one). Default builds of the six edited tests are byte-identical to
  origin/main's (riscv64-elf-gcc 16.2.0, Mac); their -DSIGIL_NO_VECTOR builds
  contain 0 vector instructions / vector CSR accesses (objdump scan).
- ACT: scripts/act4_novec_config.py derives sigil-core-novec from
  sw/act4-core (no Zve*/Zvl*, vector params dropped incl. VSSTATUS_VS_EXISTS,
  MSTATUS_VS_LEGAL_VALUES [0], Sail V support_level Disabled);
  scripts/build_act4_core.sh ACT_CONFIG=novec.
- scripts/novec_equiv.sh: invariance proof (below).
- CI: core-regression.yml job core-novec (make -C sim core-novec-quick).
- Docs: README (build configurations), docs/CORE.md (no-vector section),
  docs/SOC_AREA.md (MPW section), sw/act4-core/README.md.

