Method (as scripts/fpga_timing_equiv.sh on 53-mem-stage-pipeline): module
proofs with equiv_make / equiv_struct / equiv_simple / equiv_induct /
equiv_status -assert; sigil_core flattened with its 12 submodule instances
as black boxes paired by equiv_make (sigil_decoder and sigil_csr proven
above, the rest byte-identical to REF, checked by the script). Two renames,
no logic: g_vec.u_vregfile / g_vec.u_vec -> u_vregfile / u_vec, and the
sigil_csr HAS_VECTOR override (= its default, 1) dropped. SRAM-macro configs
read the unchanged macro models as black boxes.
Control (main vs main, same flow): sigil_core default EQUIVALENT, 10607
proven. Yosys 0.69 (Mac) cannot run this flow (equiv_induct errors "No SAT
model available" on the black boxes even for identical designs), hence 0.33.
Mutants (each must be detected; tree 6ba052d):
  M1 decoder: if (!HAS_VECTOR && vec) -> if (HAS_VECTOR && vec): sigil_decoder FAILED, 19 unproven
  M2 csr: MISA with V -> without V when HAS_VECTOR:                sigil_csr FAILED, 1 unproven
  M3 csr: mstatus_vs = HAS_VECTOR ? 0 : mstatus_vs_q:               sigil_csr FAILED, 2 unproven
  M4 core: vls_is = !HAS_VECTOR && ...:                             sigil_core FAILED, 566 unproven
  M5 core: if (!HAS_VECTOR) begin : g_vec:                          sigil_core FAILED (no vector instances to pair)
FPGA_TIMING (53-mem-stage-pipeline 4421934, behind main): the RTL diff of
this branch applied to it (conflicts resolved: sigil_csr takes both
parameters, `#(.FPGA_TIMING(FPGA_TIMING), .HAS_VECTOR(HAS_VECTOR))`; the
53 base's own vector-unit connections and no commit-trace block), lint
clean with and without SIGIL_NO_VECTOR (+SIGIL_FPGA_TIMING +SIGIL_VRF_OREG),
then REF=4421934 EXTRA_DEFS=SIGIL_FPGA_TIMING MOD_CHPARAM=FPGA_TIMING=1:
